# Auto-generated files — collapse diffs and exclude from language stats
web/package-lock.json linguist-generated=true

# Enforce LF for scripts that run inside Linux containers.
# Without this, Windows checkout converts to CRLF and breaks `exec` in the
# container entrypoint with "no such file or directory".
*.sh        text eol=lf
Dockerfile  text eol=lf
*.dockerfile text eol=lf
docker/entrypoint.sh text eol=lf

# Everything under docker/ is consumed byte-for-byte inside the image, and both
# of these break when a carriage return sneaks in:
#
#   s6-rc.d/<svc>/type   s6-rc-compile compares the whole file against the
#                        literals oneshot/longrun/bundle. Content "longrun" plus
#                        a CR is none of them, and it aborts init with
#                        "s6-rc-compile: fatal: invalid .../main-openamer/type",
#                        so every container hangs before it runs anything.
#   cont-init.d/*        same class one stage later: the shebang line resolves
#                        to an interpreter named "sh" plus a CR.
#
# Pin the whole directory rather than extensions: `type`, `run`, `finish` and
# the cont-init hooks either have no extension or are not `*.sh`. docker/ holds
# only text files today; a binary added later needs an explicit `-text`.
docker/** text eol=lf
